# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
# Android size budgets: the single source of truth read by scripts/android-size-check.sh (CI job "Android / unit tests,
# lint, debug APK", and scripts/android-perf.sh size). Plain KEY=value, no spaces, so bash can source it.
#
# Units: decimal bytes. "7.25 MB" in docs/android-perf.md is 7 250 000 B (the measured 7 131 300 B is quoted there as
# 7.13 MB = bytes / 10^6, not / 2^20), so these are exact, not rounded MiB.
#
# What is measured: the UNSIGNED release APK (R8 + resource shrinking, no zipalign/signature; signing adds about 10 kB), built with the
# CI recipe (cargo --profile android, --icf=all, llvm-strip). classes.dex is the sum of the uncompressed sizes of every classes*.dex in
# the APK. Tightened 2026-11-06 to the CI measurement at 3e81e823a (universal 7 114 124, arm64 3 539 267, dex 567 180) plus about
# 100 kB / 40 kB / 25 kB of headroom. Raising a budget needs an explanation in docs/android-perf.md (Size section), in the same commit.

# Release APK, phone + emulator ABIs (arm64-v8a + x86_64): the universal APK the updater reads.
GB_BUDGET_APK_UNIVERSAL=7215000
# Release APK, phone only (-Pgb.abis=arm64-v8a).
GB_BUDGET_APK_ARM64=3580000
# classes.dex of the release APK (after R8).
GB_BUDGET_DEX=592000
